\paragraph{Comparison of STRAP with Other Models} We compare STRAP with four benchmarks, representing a diverse range of trajectory prediction approaches, including a traditional physics-based method, LSTM-based models, and a transformer-based model. 
\begin{itemize}
    \item CV: A physics-based model that assumes that the target vehicle moves at a constant velocity.
    \item Social-LSTM (S-LSTM)\cite{b11}: An LSTM-based model that introduces a social pooling layer to aggregate the features of different vehicles.
    \item Convolutional Social-LSTM (CS-LSTM)\cite{b12}: A LSTM-based model that uses convolutional social pooling to capture interactions.
    \item STDAN\cite{b2}: A transformer-based model that considers driver's intentions.
    \item STRAP-B: Our model using basic loss function of the sum of \(\mathcal{L}_{goal}\) and \(\mathcal{L}_{traj}\).
    \item STRAP-R: Our model using the risk-scaled loss function.
\end{itemize}

