\paragraph{Datasets.} 
We evaluate on four diverse datasets to ensure robust findings across different domains: (1) \proposeddataset{}, our primary benchmark containing 580,145 audio-visual clips with fine-grained alignment annotations; (2) AudioCaps \citep{kim2019audiocaps}, featuring audio captions for AudioSet segments; (3) TVSum \citep{song2015tvsum}, containing summarization-focused video content; and (4) Ego4D \citep{grauman2022ego4d}, representing challenging egocentric perspectives.

\paragraph{Audio Encoders.} 
We comprehensively evaluate five state-of-the-art audio representation models: (1) Whisper \citep{radford2023whisper}, an ASR-focused encoder trained on 680K hours of supervised data; (2) ImageBind \citep{girdhar2023imagebind}, a joint embedding model trained on image-text-audio triplets; (3) CLAP \citep{elizalde2023clap}, trained on audio-text pairs; (4) AudioCLIP \citep{guzhov2022audioclip}, which extends CLIP's contrastive learning to audio; and (5) Wav2CLIP \citep{wu2022wav2clip}, which distills knowledge from CLIP's visual space to audio. Additionally, we evaluate our proposed \proposedaudioencoder{}, which enhances Whisper through multi-layer fusion.

\paragraph{Evaluation Method.} 
We assess performance across two key areas: \textit{cross-modal retrieval} aligned with CLIP and \textit{zero-shot text generation} with visual token substitution. For retrieval, we measure Top-$k$ Accuracy ($k \in \{1,3,10\}$) for both Audio→Video and Video→Audio retrievals. For generation quality, we use conventional NLP metrics (BLEU, ROUGE-L, BERTScore, CLIP-Score) and GPT-4o evaluation along six dimensions: audio quality, visual accuracy, coherence, reasoning, fluency, and overall usefulness.

\paragraph{Implementation Details.} 
The SoundCLIP projection networks were structured as three-layer MLPs with LayerNorm and GELU activations (1.9M parameters). For token substitution, we investigate two budget options: $k=15$ (audio-driven) and $k=150$ (vision-driven). Additional implementation details are provided in Appendix.

