\section*{Conclusion}

In this paper, we presented a Python implementation of the differential geometry of shape analysis in the module \texttt{shape} integrated in the software Geomstats. We introduced the architecture of the module and showed that it contains the essential building blocks to perform statistics and machine learning on shape data, through several code snippets. We hope that our implementation will inspire researchers to use, and contribute to, shape analysis with the \codeobj{Geomstats} library.


