\section{Proven formulas}
\label{proven-formulas}
After having found the formulas shown in the hypergraph (figure \ref{fig:hypergraph}), we proved some of them, and we list these proven formulas here. We also plan joint works with mathematicians that focus on the proofs of the formulas and their potential impact in the relevant fields of mathematics, to be submitted to mathematics journals.
This effort complements our main contribution in this work, which is concerned with the automated generation of the formulas.

In total, we proved 47 formulas of the form $a_0+b_1/(a_1+b_2/(...+b_n/(a_n+...)))$, of which 22 we showcase in this table. 6 of the formulas can be generalized to three parametric families, presented in lines 1-9. Lines 10-25 describe additional proven formulas. The proofs rely on (1) inverting Euler's continued fraction formula with parameters $h_1,h_2,f$ to (2) create an infinite sum, which we (3) translate into a hypergeometric-function form, and (4) complete the proof using known hypergeometric identities.

