Now, let us consider the vertices $u_1, u_2, \ldots, u_\ell$ on $Q$ such that, for each $r\in [\ell]$, the vertex $u_r$ is the vertex with $Q$-distance $r\cdot \ell + 1$ from $u'$ on $Q$. 
Similarly, let us consider the vertices $v_1, v_2, \ldots, v_\ell$ on $Q$ such that, for each $r\in [\ell]$, the vertex $v_r$ is the vertex with $Q$-distance $r\cdot \ell + 1$ from $v'$ on $Q$. We claim that there is a pair $(u_i, v_j)$ that satisfies property 3. 
