% \item A polynomial-time algorithm that tests if $G$ admits a \UER drawing without~internal degree-3 vertices (see \Cref{fig:crd-examples-b}). The algorithm can be adapted to preserve~a~given external face. The time complexity ranges from $O(n)$ to $O(n^5)$ based on the specific~setting.
% \item An $O(n^4)$-time algorithm that tests whether $G$ admits a \UER drawing, when the external face $f$ is prescribed and the removal of the vertices of $f$ yields a set of paths~and~cycles.
% \item An FPT algorithm, with parameter $k$ being the number of degree-3 vertices, that tests whether $G$ admits a \UER drawing. The algorithm can be adapted to preserve a prescribed external face. The time complexity of the algorithm is $O(3^k n^{4.5})$.
% \end{enumerate}
% 

\medskip All our algorithms are easily implementable and can preserve a given rotation system for the vertices, if needed. If the recognition is successful, within the same time complexity of the test, they can construct the corresponding drawing.

